<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Release-scoped upgrade data for Darpan 1.5.1.
Assembled from the generic seed files under runtime/component/darpan/data/ over the range
v1.5.0..v1.5.1, then hand-ordered. Load with: ./gradlew loadDarpanUpgradeData

This is a HOTFIX pack and it is a DELTA, not a cumulative file. It carries only what changed after
1.5.0. An environment that has not yet loaded 1.5.0 must load data/releases/1.5.0/upgrade-data.xml
FIRST — this file restates a row that release creates, and will fail on a missing parent otherwise.
prod, UAT and sm-darpan all completed 1.5.0's load and migrations on 2026-08-27, so for them this
file is the only one outstanding.

ORDERING: SourceSystemConnector before SourceSystemConnectorField. Moqui's entity-facade loader
inserts rows in DOCUMENT ORDER — it does not topologically sort — so a child ahead of its parent
fails with a raw *_ibfk_* constraint error that points nowhere near this file. The Enumeration
SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS and the connector row it parents both shipped in 1.5.0, so no Enumeration row is
needed here. release_preflight.py sorts alphabetically and WILL break the one chain that remains if
this file is regenerated. Re-order by hand afterwards.

OPERATOR IMPACT: 2 records.

  - SourceSystemConnector SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS is restated (create-or-update by primary key, so it
    changes only the named columns) with filterParameterName="sourceFilters" and a keepFieldsBase
    widened by returnWorkflowStatus. Until this loads, the rules board hides the exclusion control on
    Shopify return references entirely, and any return-status rule an operator manages to configure
    is inert.

  - SourceSystemConnectorField $.records[*].returnWorkflowStatus is new: the "Return workflow status"
    pill on the rules board for that connector.

Both records need shopify-darpan v0.6.1 or later deployed alongside. That is the component that
emits returnWorkflowStatus on return rows; against v0.6.0 the pill appears but selects a field the
extract does not contain, so every rule on it matches nothing — silently, with no error anywhere.

ONE MANUAL STEP THIS TIME — the pill was RENAMED on 2026-08-27, hours after it first shipped, from
$.records[*].returnStatus to $.records[*].returnWorkflowStatus. Shopify's own Order.returnStatus is
a DIFFERENT field holding a DIFFERENT enum (OrderReturnStatus: IN_PROGRESS, INSPECTION_COMPLETE,
NO_RETURN, RETURN_FAILED, RETURN_REQUESTED, RETURNED); this pill selects Return.status (ReturnStatus:
REQUESTED, OPEN, CLOSED, DECLINED, CANCELED). An operator on production read the docs the old name
pointed at, excluded on IN_PROGRESS, and dropped nothing.

A seed load is createOrUpdate and never deletes, so loading this file INSERTS the new pill but leaves
the old one behind, and the board would offer both — one of which no longer exists on the extract, so
a rule on it silently matches nothing forever. The old PK is declared in
SourceSystemConnectorFieldWriteSupport.RETIRED_FIELDS, which the RETIRED_FIELDS migration deletes —
but that migration is ALREADY APPLIED on every environment that ran 1.5.0's migrations, and
run#PendingMigrations skips anything already applied. It must therefore be re-run explicitly ONCE per
environment, after this file loads:

    admin.MigrationAdminServices.run#Migration  migrationId=RETIRED_FIELDS  force=true

(the Migrations screen's per-migration run with force set does the same). It is idempotent — a second
run deletes nothing. Skip it and the stale "Return status" pill stays on the rules board.

Any exclusion rule already saved against the OLD path keeps its stored expression and will match
nothing after the rename; re-add it on the new pill, with values REQUESTED,OPEN.

An environment that never loaded the few-hour-old original does not have the stale row and the forced
re-run is a no-op there. Running it anyway is safe and is the recommended default, because telling
the two cases apart from outside the database is not worth the operator's time.
-->
<entity-facade-xml type="darpan-seed">

    <!-- Shopify per-EVENT (refund or return) records for returns reconciliation. Restated from
         1.5.0 to add filterParameterName and widen keepFieldsBase. filterParameterName ADDED
         2026-08-27: this connector now carries tenant exclusion rules, so the rules board offers the
         control and the getter applies them client-side (Shopify's search syntax has no knowledge of
         tenant rules). The canonical SHOPIFY orders row still declares none and still means what it
         said. Every other column below is unchanged from 1.5.0 and is restated only because
         create-or-update writes whole rows. -->
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector
            systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS"
            extractServiceName="reconciliation.ShopifyOrderExtractionServices.extract#ShopifyOrderReturnRefs"
            dateFromParameterName="windowStart"
            dateToParameterName="windowEnd"
            expectedSourceConfigType="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS_API"
            configParameterName="shopifyAuthConfigId"
            configEntityName="darpan.shopify.ShopifyAuthConfig"
            remoteId="SHOPIFY_REMOTE"
            endpointLabel="Shopify Return References"
            systemAliases="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS,SHOPIFY_RETURNS,DAR_SYS_SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS"
            preserveWindowInstants="N"
            filterParameterName="sourceFilters"
            keepFieldsBase="refundOrReturnId,refundOrReturnType,orderId,createdAt,orderCancelledAt,refundLineEverFulfilled,returnWorkflowStatus"
            lookupServiceName="reconciliation.ShopifyOrderExtractionServices.lookup#ShopifyRefundOrReturnIds"
            lookupIdsParameterName="refundOrReturnIds"
            lookupMaxIds="10000"
            enabled="Y"/>

    <!-- The rules-board pill the connector change exists for. FKs the SourceSystemConnector
         immediately above by systemEnumId. -->
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" fieldPath="$.records[*].returnWorkflowStatus"
            label="Return workflow status" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="5"
            description="ADDED 2026-08-27, RENAMED the same day from returnStatus — see the retirement
                entry in SourceSystemConnectorFieldWriteSupport.RETIRED_FIELDS. Holds a Shopify
                ReturnStatus: REQUESTED, OPEN, CLOSED, DECLINED, CANCELED. It is NOT Shopify's
                Order.returnStatus, a different field holding an OrderReturnStatus (IN_PROGRESS,
                INSPECTION_COMPLETE, NO_RETURN, RETURN_FAILED, RETURN_REQUESTED, RETURNED) that
                aggregates a whole order for display; under the old name an operator excluded on
                IN_PROGRESS and matched nothing. Present on RETURN rows only: a REFUND row has no
                return status, so a rule on this field can never match one. Because a refunded return
                is represented by its refund's row alone, this field only ever describes an UNREFUNDED
                return — excluding OPEN excludes unrefunded OPEN returns. Exclude REQUESTED,OPEN to
                drop in-progress returns that have no OMS counterpart yet."/>

</entity-facade-xml>
